@subheading Description

Welcome to the G-Golf Customization Square.

This section is organized per customization theme: (-) GI Name
Transformation; (-) GI strip boolean result; (-) GI method short name
skip.


@subheading GI Name Transformation

In this corner of the square, we expose how you may customize G-Golf
with respect to GI Name Transformation that occurs when importing GNOME
libraries.

When G-Golf imports a GNOME library, its classes, properties, methods,
functions, types and constants are renamed (@xref{Naming Conventions}),
mainly to (a) avoid @samp{@uref{@value{UWIKI-CAMELCASE}, Camel Case}},
(b) surround class names by @samp{<} @samp{>} and (c) replace @samp{_}
(underscore) occurrences using the @samp{-} (hyphen) character.


As the context of name transformation is GNOME in general, as opposed to
GI more specifically, (all) procedures involved are named using a
@code{g-} prefix.

Here is a summary of how the name transformation happens:

@itemize
@item
Class names are obtained by calling @ref{g-name->class-name}, which
calls @ref{g-name->name};
@*@*

@item
@ref{g-name->name} first calls @ref{g-name-transform-exception?} and
returns its value if it found one, otherwise, it calls
@ref{g-studly-caps-expand};
@*@*

@item
@ref{g-studly-caps-expand}, which does the core of the job, uses
@ref{g-studly-caps-expand-token-exception?} to specially treat its
listed token exceptions.
@end itemize


@anchor{g-name-transform-exception}
@deffn Procedure g-name-transform-exception

Returns an alist.

Obtains and returns the list of GI name transform exception @code{(key
. value)} pairs. Both @code{key} and @code{value} are strings.

The GI name transform exception alist is never empty, as it is
initialized and always kept to at least contain the @code{'("GObject"
. "gobject")} pair@footnote{This is the only name for which G-Golf
maintains compatibility with Guile-GNOME (which has a long list of
exceptions)..}.

 As a consequence @ref{<gobject>} (as opposed to @code{<g-object>} is
the G-Golf class name for the base class of the GLib Object
System.

This only affects the class name though - any procedure or method name
that comes from the @code{"GObject"} namespace is transformed using the
@code{g-object} prefix, as the upstream library prefix is
@code{g_object}.
@end deffn


@anchor{g-name-transform-exception?}
@deffn Procedure g-name-transform-exception? key

Returns @code{#t} if @var{key} is a key member of the GI name transform
exception alist. Otherwise, it returns @code{#f}.
@end deffn


@anchor{g-name-transform-exception-add}
@anchor{g-name-transform-exception-remove}
@deffn Procedure g-name-transform-exception-add key value
@deffnx Procedure g-name-transform-exception-remove key

Returns nothing.

Add (remove) a @var{(key . value)} pair to (from) the GI name transform
exception alist.
@end deffn


@anchor{g-name-transform-exception-reset}
@deffn Procedure g-name-transform-exception-reset

Returns nothing.

This procedure resets the GI name transform exception alist to its
default value - which is to contain the single @code{'("GObject"
. "gobject")} pair.
@end deffn


@anchor{g-studly-caps-expand-token-exception}
@deffn Procedure g-studly-caps-expand-token-exception

Returns an alist.

Obtains and returns the list of GI studly caps expand token exception
@code{(key . value)} pairs. Both @code{key} and @code{value} are
strings.

The GI studly caps expand token exception alist is never empty, as it is
initialized and always kept to at least contain the @code{'("WebKit"
. "webkit")} pair.
@end deffn


@anchor{g-studly-caps-expand-token-exception?}
@deffn Procedure g-studly-caps-expand-token-exception? key

Returns @code{#t} if @var{key} is a key member of the GI studly caps
expand token exception alist. Otherwise, it returns @code{#f}.
@end deffn


@anchor{g-studly-caps-expand-token-exception-add}
@anchor{g-studly-caps-expand-token-exception-remove}
@deffn Procedure g-studly-caps-expand-token-exception-add key value
@deffnx Procedure g-studly-caps-expand-token-exception-remove key

Returns nothing.

Add (remove) a @var{(key . value)} pair to (from) the GI studly caps
expand token exception alist.
@end deffn


@anchor{g-studly-caps-expand-token-exception-reset}
@deffn Procedure g-studly-caps-expand-token-exception-reset

Returns nothing.

This procedure resets the GI studly caps expand token exception alist to
its default value - which is to contain the single @code{'("WebKit"
. "webkit")} pair.
@end deffn


@subheading GI Strip Boolean Result

In this corner of the square, we expose how you may customize G-Golf
with respect to GI typelib functions and methods that (1) have at least
one @code{'inout} or @code{'out} argument(s) and (2) return either
@code{#t} or @code{#f}, solely to indicate that the function or method
call was successful or not.

The default G-Golf behavior, when there is at least one @code{'inout} or
@code{'out} argument(s), is to return multiple values. The first
returned value is the function or method result, followed by the
@code{'inout} and @code{'out} values, in order of appearance in the
function or method call.

G-Golf also offers - through a series of interfaces to get, check, add,
remove and reset a list of such function or methods names - to instead
elude the function or method returned value when it is @code{#t} and
raise an exception if the returned value is @code{#f}.

Here is a concrete example, for the @code{"Clutter"} namespace and
the @code{clutter-color-from-string} procedure:

@lisp
,use (g-golf)
(gi-import "Clutter")

(clutter-color-from-string "Blue")
@result{} $2 = #t
@result{} $3 = (0 0 255 255)
@end lisp

And call it with an undefined color name:

@lisp
(clutter-color-from-string "Bluee")
@result{} $4 = #f
@result{} $5 = (0 0 0 0)
@end lisp

Now, let's add @code{clutter-color-from-string} to the list of GI
funtions and methods for which we wish to elude the result of the call
from the returned value(s), then experiment the above calls and see how
G-Golf changed the way it handles the results:

@lisp
(gi-strip-boolean-result-add clutter-color-from-string)

(clutter-color-from-string "Blue")
@result{} $7 = (0 0 255 255)
@end lisp

As expected, if we call it with an undefined color name, it will raise
an exception@footnote{Note that the raised exception message and
formatting depends on the version of guile you are using. Fwiw, this
example was produced using @code{GNU Guile 3.0.8}.}

@lisp
(clutter-color-from-string "Bluee")
@print{} ice-9/boot-9.scm:1686:16: In procedure raise-exception:
@print{}   clutter-color-from-string " failed."
@print{}
@print{} Entering a new prompt.  Type `,bt' for a backtrace or `,q' to continue.
@end lisp

G-Golf default is that the list of GI funtions and methods for which to
elude the result of the call from the returned value(s) is empty. It is
a user responsibility to fill it appropriately, for each namespace they
are importing.


@anchor{gi-strip-boolean-result}
@deffn Procedure gi-strip-boolean-result

Returns a (possibly empty) list of (symbol) name(s).

Obtains and returns the list of GI funtions and methods for which G-Golf
will elude the result of the call from the returned value(s).
@end deffn


@anchor{gi-strip-boolean-result?}
@deffn Procedure gi-strip-boolean-result? name

Returns @code{#t} if @var{name} is a member of the list of GI funtions
and methods for which G-Golf will elude the result of the call from the
returned value(s). Otherwise, it returns @code{#f}.
@end deffn


@anchor{gi-strip-boolean-result-add}
@anchor{gi-strip-boolean-result-remove}
@deffn Syntax gi-strip-boolean-result-add name @dots{}
@deffnx Syntax gi-strip-boolean-result-remove name @dots{}

Add (remove) the @var{names} to (from) the list of GI funtions and
methods for which G-Golf will elude the result of the call from the
returned value(s).
@end deffn


@anchor{gi-strip-boolean-result-reset}
@deffn Procedure gi-strip-boolean-result-reset

Resets the list of GI funtions and methods for which G-Golf will elude
the result of the call from the returned value(s) to the empty list.
@end deffn


@subheading GI Method Short Name Skip

In this corner of the square, we expose how you may customize G-Golf
with respect to GI method short name, more specifically, whether you
wish to skip the method short name creation, and doing so individually
or for all GI imported methods.

By default, as it imports a GI typelib, G-Golf creates a method short
name for each imported method, obtained by dropping the container name
(and its trailing hyphen) from the GI typelib method full/long name.

For example, the @code{<gtk-label>} class, which defines the
@code{gtk-label-get-text} method, would also define, using G-Golf's
default settings, the @code{get-text} method. To be more precise, G-Golf
would create (if it does not exist) or reuse (if it exists) the
@code{get-text} generic function, make and add a method with its
specializer(s), in this case @code{<gtk-label>}.

Now, let's add @code{gtk-label-get-text} to the list of the GI methods
for which we wish to skip the short name creation step. In this case, as
G-Golf imports the @code{GtkLabel} class, it would only create the
@code{gtk-label-get-text} method, but not the @code{get-text} method
anymore.

@anchor{gi-method-short-name-skip}
@deffn Procedure gi-method-short-name-skip

Returns a (possibly empty) list of (symbol) name(s).

Obtains and returns the list of GI method long name for which G-Golf
will skip the method short name creation step.
@end deffn


@anchor{gi-method-short-name-skip?}
@deffn Procedure gi-method-short-name-skip? name

Returns @code{#t} if @var{name} is a member of the list of GI method
long name for which G-Golf will skip the method short name creation
step. Otherwise, it returns @code{#f}.
@end deffn


@anchor{gi-method-short-name-skip-all}
@deffn Procedure gi-method-short-name-skip-all

Returns nothing.

Sets the GI method short name skip creation step to @code{'all}.
@end deffn


@anchor{gi-method-short-name-skip-add}
@anchor{gi-method-short-name-skip-remove}
@deffn Syntax gi-method-short-name-skip-add name @dots{}
@deffnx Syntax gi-method-short-name-skip-remove name @dots{}

Add (remove) the @var{names} to (from) the list of GI method long name
for which G-Golf will skip the method short name creation step.
@end deffn


@anchor{gi-method-short-name-skip-reset}
@deffn Procedure gi-method-short-name-skip-reset

Resets the list of GI method long name for which G-Golf will skip the
method short name creation step to the empty list.
@end deffn

